"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1007/springerreference_78128\",\n  \"title\": \"Weights and Measures in the Indus Valley\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1007/springerreference_78128\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1970-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1007/springerreference_78128\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"reference-entry\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer-Verlag', 'container_title': 'SpringerReference', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'reference-entry', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1007'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1080/00438243.1997.9980377\",\n  \"title\": \"Trade and technology of the Indus Valley: New insights from Harappa, Pakistan\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jonathan M. Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1080/00438243.1997.9980377\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1997-10-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1080/00438243.1997.9980377\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 76,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Informa UK Limited', 'container_title': 'World Archaeology', 'volume': '29', 'issue': '2', 'page': '262-280', 'issn': ['0043-8243', '1470-1375'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '301', 'prefix': '10.1080'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1007/978-94-007-7747-7_8938\",\n  \"title\": \"Weights and Measures in the Indus Valley\",\n  \"authors\": \"Shigeo Iwata\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1007/978-94-007-7747-7_8938\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2016-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-7747-7_8938\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer Netherlands', 'container_title': 'Encyclopaedia of the History of Science, Technology, and Medicine in Non-Western Cultures', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '4473-4474', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9789400777460', '9789400777477'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1007'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1007/978-1-4020-4425-0_8938\",\n  \"title\": \"Weights and Measures in the Indus Valley\",\n  \"authors\": \"Shigeo Iwata\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1007/978-1-4020-4425-0_8938\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2008-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4020-4425-0_8938\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 8,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer Netherlands', 'container_title': 'Encyclopaedia of the History of Science, Technology, and Medicine in Non-Western Cultures', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '2254-2255', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9781402045592', '9781402044250'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1007'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.3406/paleo.1991.4553\",\n  \"title\": \"Ornament Styles of the Indus Valley Tradition : Evidence from Recent Excavations at Harappa, Pakistan\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jonathan Mark Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>Recent excavations at Harappa and Mehrgarh, as well as other sites in Pakistan and India have provided new opportunities to study the ornaments of the Indus Civilization. A brief discussion of the methodologies needed for the study of Indus ornaments is presented along with examples of how Indus artisans combined precious metals, stone beads, shell and faience to form elaborate ornaments. Many of these ornament styles were also copied in more easily obtained materials such as steatite or terra-cotta. The social and ritual implications of specific ornaments are examined through their archaeological context and comparisons with the function of specific ornaments are recorded in the ancient texts and folk traditions of South Asia.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.3406/paleo.1991.4553\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1991-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.3406/paleo.1991.4553\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 41,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'PERSEE Program', 'container_title': 'Paléorient', 'volume': '17', 'issue': '2', 'page': '79-98', 'issn': ['0153-9345'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '2000', 'prefix': '10.3406'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.23797/9783529035425\",\n  \"title\": \"Bronze Age Weights from Mesopotamia, Iran &amp; Greater Indus Valley\",\n  \"authors\": \"Enrico Ascalone\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>In this volume Enrico Ascalone presents more than 2000 weights, potential weights and other objects – mostly unpublished so far – from 20 Bronze Age sites in Iraq, Iran and India. It includes ca. 750 weights from Susa in south-western Iran and nearly 900 weights from Dholavira, Kutch district, in India. The typology, material, archaeological context and metrology of the objects is discussed. For the first time a large number of weights from the Mature Harappan culture is presented in detail. The investigations were made possible by various partners in the Iran, India and France (Louvre) and were funded by the ERC-2014-CoG 'WEIGHTANDVALUE: Weight metrology and its economic and social impact on Bronze Age Europe, West and South Asia' [Grant no. 648055].</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.23797/9783529035425\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2022-12-19T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.23797/9783529035425\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 4,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Wachholtz', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9783529035425', '9783529035425'], 'crossref_type': 'book', 'member': '3821', 'prefix': '10.23797'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1557/proc-267-495\",\n  \"title\": \"A New Look at Stone Drills of the Indus Valley Tradition\",\n  \"authors\": \"J. Mark Kenoyer; Massimo Vidale\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:title>ABSTRACT</jats:title><jats:p>Drilling technology of the Indus Valley Tradition was highly specialized and various types of chert and jasper were used to drill different types of materials. Earlier studies used primarily macroscopic observations to define features such as the manufacturing technique of drills, the raw materials and the mechanics of drilling. These generalizations can be revised given the discovery of important workshop areas and the availability of SEM, XRD and electron microprobe analysis. This paper will summarize the current state of. drilling research and define two categories of drills that were used in antiquity; <jats:italic>tapered cylindrical drills</jats:italic> and <jats:italic>constricted cylindrical drills.</jats:italic> Directions for future research on the relationship between drilling and other contemporaneous technologies are discussed.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1557/proc-267-495\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1992-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1557/proc-267-495\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 24,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer Science and Business Media LLC', 'container_title': 'MRS Proceedings', 'volume': '267', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': ['0272-9172', '1946-4274'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1557'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.29\",\n  \"title\": \"Invisible Value or Tactile Value?\",\n  \"authors\": \"Heather M.-L. Miller; Jonathan Mark Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.29\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2018-08-13T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.29\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 3,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'Walking with the Unicorn: Social Organization and Material Culture in Ancient South Asia', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '389-394', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9781784919184'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1007/bf00978474\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Valley Tradition of Pakistan and western India\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jonathan Mark Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1007/bf00978474\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1991-12-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"http://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BF00978474.pdf\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1007/bf00978474\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 81,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer Science and Business Media LLC', 'container_title': 'Journal of World Prehistory', 'volume': '5', 'issue': '4', 'page': '331-385', 'issn': ['0892-7537', '1573-7802'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1007'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1515/9783110816433.213\",\n  \"title\": \"10. Interaction systems, specialised crafts and culture change: The Indus Valley Tradition and the Indo-Gangetic Tradition in South Asia\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jonathan Mark Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1515/9783110816433.213\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1970-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110816433.213\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'DE GRUYTER', 'container_title': 'The Indo-Aryans of Ancient South Asia', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '374', 'prefix': '10.1515'}\"\n}"
